# Session Schema Standards

## Events are append-only
Never modify or delete a recorded event. The event log is an immutable audit trail.

## Required fields on every event
All SessionEvent objects must have: id, type, timestamp, data.
```python
# ✅ GOOD
event = SessionEvent(
    id=str(uuid.uuid4()),
    type=EventType.TOOL_CALL,
    timestamp=datetime.utcnow(),
    data={"tool": "read_file", "params": {"path": "src/main.py"}}
)

# ❌ BAD — missing id and timestamp
event = {"type": "tool_call", "data": {"tool": "read_file"}}
```

## Session ID format
Use `session-YYYYMMDD-NNN` format. Don't use random UUIDs for session IDs — they're not human-readable in file listings.

## Artifacts by reference
Store artifact paths, not artifact content, in the session JSON. Large content in events causes performance issues.
